---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const manifest = `{
  "manifest_version": 1,
  "id": "dev.example.workouts",
  "name": "Example Workouts",
  "homepage": "https://workouts.example",
  "redirect_uris": [
    "https://workouts.example/auth/mdbase/callback"
  ],
  "requirements": {
    "contracts": []
  }
}`;

const install = `pnpm add @mdbase/connect
pnpm add -D @mdbase/connect-dev`;

const client = `import {
  MdbaseConnect,
  type JsonObject
} from "@mdbase/connect";

export interface Workout extends JsonObject {
  type: "workout";
  title: string;
  completed?: boolean;
}

export const mdbase = new MdbaseConnect<Workout>({
  serverUrl: "https://connect.mdbase.dev",
  manifest: new URL("/.well-known/mdbase-app.json", location.origin).href,
  redirectUri: new URL("/auth/mdbase/callback", location.origin).href
});`;

const connectButton = `import { mdbase } from "./connect";

export async function connectCollection() {
  await mdbase.authorize({
    operations: ["describe", "read", "query", "update"],
    returnTo: location.pathname + location.search
  });
  // authorize() navigates to Connect and does not return.
}`;

const callback = `import { mdbase } from "./connect";

export async function completeMdbaseCallback() {
  const { connection, returnTo = "/" } =
    await mdbase.completeAuthorization(location.href);
  const destination = new URL(returnTo, location.origin);
  destination.searchParams.set("collection", connection.collectionId);
  history.replaceState({}, "", destination);
  return connection; // Permanently bound to this collection.
}`;

const query = `import { mdbase } from "./connect";
import { unwrapOperation } from "@mdbase/connect";

const collectionId = new URL(location.href).searchParams.get("collection");
const collection = collectionId ? mdbase.connection(collectionId) : null;
if (!collection) throw new Error("Choose a collection.");

const page = unwrapOperation(await collection.query({
  types: ["workout"],
  where: 'completed != true',
  order_by: [{ field: "title", direction: "asc" }],
  limit: 50
}));

const first = page.results[0];
if (first) {
  unwrapOperation(await collection.update({
    path: first.path,
    patch: { completed: true },
    if_revision: first.revision
  }));
}`;

const validate = `mdbase-connect-dev validate-manifest \\
  public/.well-known/mdbase-app.json`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart"
  description="Connect a browser application, complete authorization, query records, and make a revision-safe update."
  active="quickstart"
  headings={[
    { href: "#manifest", label: "1. Add a manifest" },
    { href: "#install", label: "2. Install" },
    { href: "#client", label: "3. Create the client" },
    { href: "#authorize", label: "4. Authorize" },
    { href: "#callback", label: "5. Complete callback" },
    { href: "#operate", label: "6. Use operations" }
  ]}
>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Private-beta requirement</strong>
    <p>
      The production service currently accepts private-beta accounts. Use one
      of those accounts or the repository's local stack for this guide.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="manifest">1. Add a bundled application manifest</h2>
  <p>
    Save this file at <code>public/.well-known/mdbase-app.json</code>. The SDK
    loads the file from your own application and posts it inline during
    registration. The control plane receives the canonical JSON from the SDK.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={manifest} language="json" label="public/.well-known/mdbase-app.json" />
  <p>
    The reverse-domain ID and name are display metadata. An approved grant binds
    the canonical manifest content to the application installation that
    completed authorization.
  </p>

  <h2 id="install">2. Install the SDK and validator</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} language="sh" label="Terminal" />
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>The packages are awaiting their first npm publication.</strong>
    <p>
      The commands above are the public-beta installation path. Current
      development builds <code>@mdbase/connect</code>,
      {" "}<code>@mdbase/connect-protocol</code>, and
      {" "}<code>@mdbase/connect-dev</code> from the
      {" "}<a href="https://github.com/mdbase-dev/mdbase-connect">Connect repository</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
  <p>Validate the bundled file during development and CI:</p>
  <CodeBlock code={validate} language="sh" label="Terminal" />
  <p>
    For a loopback development homepage and callback, add
    {" "}<code>--allow-local</code>. Production web homepages, icons, and
    browser callbacks use HTTPS. Native callbacks may use a private scheme
    derived from the application ID.
  </p>

  <h2 id="client">3. Create one Connect client</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={client} language="ts" label="src/connect.ts" />
  <p>
    Keep this manager stable. It owns the set of saved connections and returns
    a separate collection-bound client for each one. Feature and repository
    code should receive that bound client, never ambient “current collection”
    state.
  </p>

  <h2 id="authorize">4. Start authorization from a user action</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={connectButton} language="ts" label="src/connect-button.ts" />
  <p>
    Connect shows compatible collections and asks the user to approve the exact
    operations. The collection description becomes available after approval.
  </p>

  <h2 id="callback">5. Complete the callback</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={callback} language="ts" label="src/mdbase-callback.ts" />
  <p>
    Call this once on the exact callback route listed in the manifest. PKCE is
    mandatory. On success, the client stores the grant-bound authorization and
    returns the newly approved collection-bound connection.
  </p>

  <h2 id="operate">6. Query and update with a revision</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={query} language="ts" label="src/workouts.ts" />
  <p>
    Query results include a revision token. Pass it as
    {" "}<code>if_revision</code> when changing the record so a concurrent edit
    cannot be silently overwritten.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Use a stable collection ID in app URLs.</strong>
    <p>
      A query parameter such as <code>?collection=&lt;id&gt;</code> works on
      static hosts, survives refreshes, and makes a view bookmarkable. Treat an
      explicit ID as authoritative: if it is not saved, show the chooser or
      reconnect that ID instead of silently opening another collection. Names
      are display text and can change.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Resolve domain fields from the contract descriptor.</strong>
    <p>
      Generic apps can use declared mdbase types directly. Domain applications
      should read the contract descriptors returned by <code>describe()</code>{" "}
      or use an adapter maintained by the owning application.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="button-row" style="margin-top: 2rem">
    <a class="button button--primary" href="/sdk/manifest/">Design the manifest</a>
    <a class="button" href="/sdk/portable-apps/">Build one downloaded file</a>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
